<title>UK: World Bank adds 1.0 trillion lire to 20-year zero.</title>
<headline>World Bank adds 1.0 trillion lire to 20-year zero.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to 3.0 trillion lire, joint lead managers Credito Italian and Citibank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT    1.0 TRLN LIRE COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    07.NOV.16</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  25.753    PAY DATE    20.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    23.903    SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    N/A</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (M) 5-50-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.15	SELL CONC  1.85	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> NOTES	TOTAL SIZE NOW 3.0 TRLN LIRE.</p>
<p>		PAPER PREVIOUSLY LAUNCHED ON OCTOBER 02, 21 AND 28.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
